  "externalFindings": {
    "identity": "Leiden BA-RUS, RIO 50855, Dutch programme language with selected English-language modules and Russian language instruction. 2026–2027 catalogue and OER effective 1 September 2026.",
    "route": "Both formal tracks use a common first year and 20 EC of selected specialization per year thereafter. The programme-specific OER Article 2.2 and BA-RUS tree list Politics, History and Economics first. The same track is used in both years.",
    "year2": "40 EC common plus 20 EC track. 5642V017Y is 10 EC of assessed language immersion in Daugavpils after the first year, and 5642V019Y is a distinct 5 EC art history unit taught there. 5642V023Y is a distinct 5 EC Leiden language course with assessments before departure, not a duplicate of the stay.",
    "year3": "20 EC track, 10 EC Bachelor’s Thesis and separately required 0 EC thesis seminar, plus KRB15S1 and KRB15S2, 15 EC each in different semesters. Elective placeholders stay generic, with applicable level, approval and nonoverlap requirements.",
    "progression": "OER 4.2.1 sets earlier grammar and acquisition gates, Reading 2A before 2B, first year before abroad, and first year plus relevant second-year seminars before thesis. Thesis catalogue asks for years one and two completed, with supervised work assessed on the final submission and substantial Russian-language sources. The illustrated route completes both years before thesis and seminar, satisfying both sources. OER 2.3 contains inconsistent CEFR statements, so no exact exit level is claimed."
  },
